<file path="MIGRATION_NOTES.md">
# Migration Notes — Rental (React/Vite) → Next.js (chat-system)

All of the old `rental_room` React + Vite pages/components were ported into this
Next.js app (`next-frontend`) and converted from **JSX → TSX**. The existing
real-time chat was kept intact and moved under `/chat`.

## Run it

```bash
# Frontend
cd next-frontend
npm install
npm run dev          # http://localhost:3000

# Backend (chat) — separate terminal
cd node-backend
npm install
npm start            # http://localhost:5001  (needs MySQL/XAMPP, see its README)
```

The chat frontend talks to the backend via `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`
(defaults to `http://localhost:5001`). Set it in `next-frontend/.env.local` if needed.

## Routes

| Route                 | Component (was)                          |
|-----------------------|------------------------------------------|
| `/`                   | Homepage (rental landing)                |
| `/signin`             | Login (`Login.jsx`)                      |
| `/get-started`        | GetStarted (`GetStarted.jsx`)            |
| `/landlord`           | Landlord_Navbar                          |
| `/tenant`             | Tenant_Navbar                            |
| `/tenant-booking`     | MyBookings (`MyBookings.jsx`)            |
| `/search`             | Search (`Search.jsx`)                    |
| `/filter-properties`  | Filterproperties (`Filterproperties.jsx`)|
| `/reservations`       | MyReservations (`MyReservations.jsx`)    |
| `/chat`               | Chat (was `/`)                           |
| `/chat/login`         | Chat login (was `/login`)                |
| `/chat/register`      | Chat register (was `/register`)          |

## What changed during the port

- **Routing:** `react-router-dom` (`BrowserRouter`, `Routes`, `Route`, `NavLink`)
  removed. Each page is now an App Router route under `app/…/page.tsx`, and
  `NavLink to=…` became `next/link` `<Link href=…>`. The chat pages' internal
  redirects were updated to the new `/chat/*` paths.
- **Chat moved to `/chat`** so the rental landing page can own `/`.
- **Components** live in `components/layout`, `components/ui`, `components/pages`.
  Route files in `app/` are thin wrappers that render them.
- **Images:** moved from `src/assets` to `public/assets` and referenced by URL
  (e.g. `/assets/left_img.png`) instead of static imports — the standard Next.js
  approach for plain `<img>` tags.
- **Client vs server components:** files using `useState`/handlers now start with
  `"use client"` (PropertyCard, the navbars, GetStarted, Login, MyBookings,
  Filterproperties, MyReservations). Purely presentational ones (Homepage, Navbar,
  Footer, CardList, Search) stay as server components.
- **JSX → TSX fixes:** raw-HTML attributes in inline SVGs (`class`, `stroke-width`,
  `code-path`, …) converted to valid JSX (`className`, `strokeWidth`, removed), and
  event handlers / state given proper types. `npx tsc --noEmit` passes.
- **Small fixes:** two CSS imports pointed at non-existent filenames
  (`SearchProperties.css`, `Reservations.css`) — corrected to the real files.
  The tenant sidebar was internally named `Landlord_Navbar`; renamed to
  `Tenant_Navbar` and its role label set to "Tenant". The floating chat button on
  `/search` now links to `/chat`.
- **Theme:** `globals.css` uses the rental light background; the `/chat` pages keep
  their own dark (`bg-zinc-950`) backgrounds, so both look correct.

> Note: `npm run build` needs internet access the first time to fetch the Geist
> Google Font used in `app/layout.tsx`.
